---
import { WINDOW_NAMES } from "../../data/clear-instruments";
---

<section
  class="clear-instrument scale"
  id="scale"
  data-instrument="scale"
  aria-labelledby="scale-title"
>
  <header class="instrument-heading">
    <p class="code">03 / THE SCALE</p>
    <span class="instrument-state" data-scale-state>
      PARTIAL
    </span>
  </header>
  <div class="scale-heading">
    <h2 id="scale-title">
      An event.
      <br />
      <em>Or a pattern?</em>
    </h2>
    <p class="field-invitation">
      Pull the field sideways.
      <br />
      Let more time enter.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="scale-window">
    <span class="code">OBSERVATION WINDOW</span>
    <output data-scale-window>1 SECOND</output>
  </div>
  <div
    class="phenomenon scale-field"
    data-scale-field
    role="slider"
    tabindex="0"
    aria-label="Observation window, drag sideways from one second to one year"
    aria-valuemin="0"
    aria-valuemax="4"
    aria-valuenow="0"
    aria-valuetext="One second"
  >
    <svg viewBox="0 0 1000 390" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true">
      <defs>
        <linearGradient id="scale-fill" x2="0" y2="1">
          <stop stop-color="#88b9ca" stop-opacity=".18" />
          <stop offset="1" stop-color="#88b9ca" stop-opacity="0" />
        </linearGradient>
      </defs>
      <g class="scale-grid">
        <path d="M35 70H965M35 180H965M35 290H965M35 40V305M965 40V305" />
        <text x="8" y="74">
          1
        </text>
        <text x="8" y="294">
          0
        </text>
      </g>
      <path class="scale-area" data-scale-area />
      <path class="scale-trace" data-scale-trace />
      <line
        class="scale-cursor"
        data-scale-cursor
        x1="35"
        x2="35"
        y1="40"
        y2="305"
      />
      <g class="scale-ruler">
        <path d="M35 345H965M35 335V355M267.5 335V355M500 335V355M732.5 335V355M965 335V355" />
        <circle data-scale-handle cx="35" cy="345" r="9" />
      </g>
      <text
        class="scale-axis"
        data-scale-axis
        x="965"
        y="325"
        text-anchor="end"
      >
        1 SECOND
      </text>
    </svg>
  </div>
  <div
    class="scale-stops"
    role="group"
    aria-label="Choose an observation window"
  >
    {WINDOW_NAMES.map((name, index) => (
      <button
        type="button"
        data-scale-stop={index}
        aria-pressed={index === 0 ? "true" : "false"}
      >
        {name}
      </button>
    ))}
  </div>
  <div class="field-foot">
    <span>ILLUSTRATIVE ACTIVITY / NORMALISED 0–1</span>
    <output data-scale-bin>240 BIN AVERAGES</output>
  </div>
  <div class="revelation" aria-live="polite">
    <p class="signal" data-scale-signal>
      CHANGE THE SCALE
    </p>
    <p class="revelation-line" data-scale-reveal>
      A fragment. Not the whole pattern.
    </p>
    <p class="revelation-detail" data-scale-detail>
      One fixed analytic record. Only the observation window changes.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="interaction-record">
    <span class="code">YOUR PATH THROUGH THE INSTRUMENT</span>
    <svg
      viewBox="0 0 600 64"
      aria-label="Your recent observation-window choices"
    >
      <path class="interaction-baseline" d="M10 50H590" />
      <path data-interaction-path />
      <g data-interaction-points />
    </svg>
    <p data-interaction-note>No exploration recorded yet.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="instrument-notes">
    <a href="/models/from-reaction-to-pattern.html">
      OPEN MODEL / FROM REACTION TO PATTERN ↗
    </a>
    <details>
      <summary>UNSEAL SCALE NOTES</summary>
      <p>
        This synthetic signal combines oscillations at 0.22 seconds, 12 seconds,
        one day, 28 days and one year, plus a small linear drift. It is an
        illustrative construction, not a scientific dataset. Thirty days is used
        for the month window; a year here is 365.25 days.
      </p>
      <p>
        Every view integrates the same function into 240 bin averages. Fine
        variation is compressed as the window grows. A pattern can survive that
        compression while its mechanism disappears. Pattern is not cause.
      </p>
      <p>
        The small path records your actual choices in this session, up to the
        latest 24. It resets on reload and is not transmitted or stored. The
        instrument’s offered scales influence which patterns you look for:
        systems train participants.
      </p>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>
